$ flow-connector-vmm
flow-connector-vmm: Run one connector in a micro-VM.
flow-connector-vmm:
flow-connector-vmm: Usage: flow-connector-vmm <COMMAND>
flow-connector-vmm:
flow-connector-vmm: Commands:
flow-connector-vmm:   run            Run one connector in a micro-VM. Does not return: libkrun takes over the process and exits with the guest workload's code
flow-connector-vmm:   check-launch   Check shared launch prerequisites without creating resources
flow-connector-vmm:   print-ruleset  Compile a policy into its nftables ruleset and write it to stdout
flow-connector-vmm:   boundary       Install, verify or remove the host's boundary around every VMM bridge. Runs in the host's network namespace, never in a VMM container
flow-connector-vmm:   help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
flow-connector-vmm:
flow-connector-vmm: Options:
flow-connector-vmm:   -h, --help  Print help

$ flow-connector-vmm boundary install
ok: boundary Install

$ flow-connector-vmm boundary verify
ok: boundary Verify

$ flow-connector-vmm boundary remove
ok: boundary Remove

$ flow-connector-vmm boundary
flow-connector-vmm: Install, verify or remove the host's boundary around every VMM bridge. Runs in the host's network namespace, never in a VMM container
flow-connector-vmm:
flow-connector-vmm: Usage: flow-connector-vmm boundary <COMMAND>
flow-connector-vmm:
flow-connector-vmm: Commands:
flow-connector-vmm:   install  Replace both tables in one transaction, then verify them. Fails, having installed them, if VMM bridges already existed while a table was absent: those VMMs ran without the boundary and must be replaced
flow-connector-vmm:   verify   Exit zero only if both tables are exactly those this binary installs
flow-connector-vmm:   remove   Delete both tables. Refused while any VMM bridge exists
flow-connector-vmm:   help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
flow-connector-vmm:
flow-connector-vmm: Options:
flow-connector-vmm:   -h, --help  Print help

